  <text>
    <body>
      <p>In a quiet room, a group gathers around a desk and speaks about <rs type="keyword" ref="#secular-humanism">human life</rs>, reason, and the common good. The voices are steady and the paper is worn.</p>
      <p>Some remarks are sharp, others are soft, but all of them move toward a practical question: what can people know, and what can they reasonably do together? <rs type="keyword" ref="#atheism-and-science">Observation</rs> appears in the middle of the exchange.</p>
      <p>The answer remains modest, built from simple language and ordinary scenes. <rs type="keyword" ref="#naturalism">Visible reality</rs> is the final frame. <gap></gap></p>
    </body>
  </text>
